Carried over from the July 2026 review (docs/review-2026-07.md), which is
now closed.  Full reasoning for each is in that document.

FAQ:
-- Two links to caricesarotti.com files are dead (the site itself is fine,
   these two PDFs are gone).  Was C1 in the review.
-- mhsmustangnews.com article is gone; you said to leave it for now.  Was C2.

External links:
-- 8 dead pages and 3 dead hosts still unfixed from the link scan.  Run
   `rake external` to list them again.  Was C5.

Technical, the only item left from the review (#10):
-- Self-host jQuery and FontAwesome instead of loading them from CDNs.
   Closes three published jQuery CVEs and removes a supply-chain vector.
   Roughly an afternoon.
-- Jekyll 3.10 -> 4.x.  Needs building in GitHub Actions instead of Pages'
   legacy builder, which also retires the live branch as a deploy
   mechanism.  Deliberately deferred until the workflow feels routine.
-- v1.jthaler.net, v2.jthaler.net and wedding.jthaler.net serve self-signed
   certificates, so those 7 links cannot move to https from this repo.
   Needs a real certificate wherever they are hosted.  The only remaining
   http:// links with an owner who can fix them.

Repository:
-- ~1.9 GB of old _site build output is still in git history.  Removing it
   means rewriting history, which breaks every existing clone.  Was the
   second half of #5.
-- _data/mentoring.yml holds contact details for 78 people in a public
   repo, left as-is by your decision.  Was 1b.